{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Cloud's `RunawayPaginationError` is swallowed by `fetch_snapshot`'s three enrichment fail-opens\n\n## Claim\n\nFound in ticket 18a4's Phase-1 parity census (the fetcher-boundary axis).\n\nDEFECT. Bug cabc's fix (ab7f, commit 30c522cde9) added `RunawayPaginationError` to Cloud's\n`adapters/jira/acli_graph.py:29` and made its three readers re-raise it past their OWN fail-open\nhandlers (`acli_graph.py:304, 394, 477`). That re-raise gets the error out of the transport — and\nstraight into `fetcher.fetch_snapshot`'s three broad `except Exception` enrichment handlers\n(parent `fetcher.py:625`, comment `:672`, issuelink `:712`), which log a warning and degrade.\n\n## Proven root cause (runtime-confirmed; see the RCA comment)\n\n`RunawayPaginationError` subclasses `RuntimeError`, NOT the core stall type. Live MRO:\n\n    (RunawayPaginationError, RuntimeError, Exception, BaseException, object)\n    issubclass(RunawayPaginationError, BackendPaginationStallError) == False\n\nThe three fetcher re-raise clauses match on the CORE type\n(`except BackendPaginationStallError: raise` at `fetcher.py:621, 668, 708`), so they MISS Cloud's\nerror and control falls to the broad `except Exception` beneath each. Driving the real\n`fetch_snapshot` with a stub whose `get_parent_map` raises `RunawayPaginationError` produced\n`WARNING ... parent enrichment failed (RunawayPaginationError(...)); snapshot written without\nparent data (degraded)` and a written snapshot — no propagation. A stalled Cloud cursor therefore\nstill yields a silently degraded snapshot that the differ treats as authoritative (missing parents\nread as parentless; missing issuelinks read as \"no links\", so link removals become undetectable).\n\nIntended behaviour is stated authoritatively at `_backend.py:49-70` (\"Readers must re-raise this\nPAST their fail-open handlers\", naming bug cabc as an instance of the class), `acli_graph.py:29-38`,\nand `fetcher.py:511-516`. cabc's fix is incomplete at the layer above the transport.\n\n## Fix\n\nTicket 18a4 fixed exactly this hole on the DC side and built the mechanism this ticket needs:\n`rebar_reconciler._backend.BackendPaginationStallError` (core, so `fetcher` can name it without\nimporting `adapters/`), plus `except BackendPaginationStallError: raise` clauses already in place\nahead of all three fetcher enrichment handlers.\n\nOne-line change: make Cloud's error subclass the core one —\n`class RunawayPaginationError(BackendPaginationStallError)` in `acli_graph.py`. The three fetcher\nre-raise clauses then cover Cloud automatically. Keeping the Cloud-specific name preserves every\nexisting `except RunawayPaginationError` site and its tests unedited; `BackendPaginationStallError`\nitself subclasses `RuntimeError`, so `except RuntimeError` sites are unaffected too. Adapters\nimporting core is the established direction (`jira_datacenter/_base.py:19` already does it).\n\nNOT folded into 18a4 deliberately: this changes observable behaviour on the CLOUD surface (stalls\nthat previously degraded now abort the pass), which another work stream owns.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A stalled Cloud cursor propagates out of `fetch_snapshot` instead of degrading: a\n      token-repeating Cloud stub driven through the REAL `fetch_snapshot` raises, for each of the\n      three enrichment readers (`get_parent_map`, `get_comment_map`, `get_issuelinks_map`).\n      Proof: `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py`\n- [ ] `issubclass(RunawayPaginationError, BackendPaginationStallError)` is `True`, and\n      `RuntimeError` remains in its MRO so existing `except RuntimeError` sites still catch it.\n      Proof: asserted in the same test module.\n- [ ] Existing `except RunawayPaginationError` sites and their tests pass UNEDITED.\n      Proof: `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` with no edits to the pre-existing test bodies.\n- [ ] Ordinary (non-stall) enrichment failures still fail open and write a degraded snapshot\n      (negative control: a plain `RuntimeError` from an enrichment reader must NOT propagate).\n      Proof: negative-control case in the same test module.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED-first held-out test added to\n  `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py`: a token-repeating Cloud\n  REST stub driven through the real `fetcher.fetch_snapshot` (loaded from source, `_load_acli`\n  patched), parameterized over all three enrichment readers, asserting the stall escapes. Verified\n  failing before the fix and passing after; mutation-checked by restoring the `RuntimeError` base.\n- Negative control in the same module: an ordinary `RuntimeError` enrichment fault still degrades\n  and writes a snapshot carrying the base scan's issues.\n- Regression: `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`, plus `make lint` and `make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785891908236639001,"uuid":"9f842dc0-d77d-439e-8b16-c8a6c7da0faf"}